From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chris Sotraidis <56282582+chrissotraidis@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 06:06:55 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] port: keep wide string scans out of the C library's wcslen

-fshort-wchar is mandatory here: prelude.h rejects a build without it, and six files cast L"..." literals to const unsigned short*. It also makes a plain unsigned short scan ABI-compatible with wchar_t, so clang's loop-idiom recognition rewrote every wide string scan into a call to the C library's wcslen. macOS has no 16-bit wcslen -- libSystem's walks 32-bit units -- so each rewritten scan came back with half the true length and could read past the end of its buffer.

Eight such scans existed in seven translation units, all reached through nlStrLen<unsigned short>. The wrong length then sized the __builtin_alloca and nlMalloc buffers in TLTextInstance::Render and FontCharString, and left nlTextBox's row table non-monotonic, so nlFont::DrawString computed a negative glyph count and its alloca blew the stack (EXC_BAD_ACCESS / KERN_PROTECTION_FAILURE from ___chkstk_darwin).

-fno-builtin-wcslen leaves those scans as the plain loops they are written as, which is 16-bit correct and no slower.
---
 smstrikers-port/CMakeLists.txt | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/smstrikers-port/CMakeLists.txt b/smstrikers-port/CMakeLists.txt
index 34a17d6..06114eb 100644
--- a/smstrikers-port/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/smstrikers-port/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -165,6 +165,13 @@ if(MSVC)
         # everywhere else.
         /clang:-Werror=pointer-to-int-cast
         /clang:-Werror=void-pointer-to-int-cast
+        # -fshort-wchar is mandatory here (prelude.h rejects a build without it), and it
+        # also makes a plain `unsigned short` scan ABI-compatible with wchar_t. clang's
+        # loop-idiom recognition then lowers such a scan to the C library's wcslen, but
+        # macOS has no 16-bit wcslen: libSystem's walks 32-bit units, so each scan came
+        # back with half the true length and could read past the end of its buffer.
+        # Keep every wide scan a plain loop.
+        /clang:-fno-builtin-wcslen
         $<$<BOOL:${STRIKERS_ASAN}>:-fsanitize=address>
     )
 else()
@@ -175,6 +182,9 @@ else()
         -fno-strict-aliasing
         -fsigned-char
         -Wno-invalid-offsetof
+        # See the MSVC branch above: without this, -fshort-wchar makes clang rewrite a
+        # 16-bit string scan into Darwin's 32-bit wcslen, which reports half a length.
+        -fno-builtin-wcslen
         $<$<BOOL:${STRIKERS_ASAN}>:-fsanitize=address>
         $<$<BOOL:${STRIKERS_ASAN}>:-fno-omit-frame-pointer>
     )
